<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lands of Overmaas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lands of Overmaas were territories east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maastricht">Maastricht</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a>: the lordships of Valkenburg, Dalhem and 's-Hertogenrade (Herzogenrath), often counted together with the neighbouring Duchy of Limburg. They were ruled by the dukes of Brabant from the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and later by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>. Disputed in the Eighty Years' War, they were divided between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> by the Partition Treaty of 1661.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lands-of-overmaas.jpg" alt="Lands of Overmaas" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chipmunkdavis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Locator_Lands_of_Overmaas_(1350).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
